    "https://stmichaels-ibukjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_2/job/65": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Dispatcher - Saint Michael's College Careers Skip to main content. College Home Employee Benefits Human Resource Office Diversity & Inclusion sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Dispatcher Colchester, VT, United States Responsibilities The Public Safety at Saint Michael's College invites applications for a full time Dispatcher. The College is seeking a qualified and experienced individual to serve as the first point of contact for callers and emergency communications. In this role, you will answer and direct incoming calls, monitor and respond to campus emergency calls, gather critical information from callers, and notify the appropriate departments for timely response. The ideal candidate will remain calm under pressure, exercise sound judgment, and maintain strict confidentiality when handling sensitive information. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Answers all incoming calls and directs to the appropriate party quickly, accurately, and    professionally Receives all calls for Public Safety, Facilities, and Student Life Oversees the key sign-out for the Saint Michael's College vehicles and vendors Monitors alarms for the HVAC department, fire detection systems, and panic and intruder systems.  Notifies appropriate resources when alarms are received Monitors door access system Monitors camera system and reviews archived camera footage Receives calls from online tip service and responds to them accordingly Enters all the log reports for Public Safety, and LiveSafe accurately and professionally; retrieves information for these units as requested Questions callers to determine nature of problem, type of response needed, and notifies the appropriate department Sees the value of cultural, ethnic, gender, and other individual differences in people. Helps to create an environment of learning about, valuing, encouraging, and supporting differences Assists in the training of new employees Sends out alerts on campus notification systems Assists walk-ins Monitors emergency calls from campus and notifies the appropriate departments The salary range for this position is $20/hr. For the full job description, click here. Schedule: This position follows a rotating schedule consisting of 12-hour shifts. We recognize that people assess their skills and experience differently. Studies have shown that some candidates may hesitate to apply for a position unless they feel they meet every qualification listed. However, many of the skills and responsibilities in this role can be developed on the job. If you believe you could bring value to our students and community and meet most of what we’re looking for, we encourage you to apply. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Benefits include health, dental, vision, employer-paid life and disability insurance, voluntary life, critical illness and accident insurance options, parental leave, flexible spending accounts (healthcare and dependent care), 401(k), generous paid time off, paid holidays, employee and dependent tuition benefits, employee and family assistance program, well-being programs and opportunities, discounted gym membership, paid volunteer time, use of the athletic facilities and the library, and countless opportunities to attend presentations, lectures, and other campus activities. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Prior working experience preferred Reads and interprets documents such as operating instructions, procedure manuals, and College policies to guide own behavior May need to spend substantial time on the telephone or in meetings to gather necessary information and plan projects May need to respond to questions and solve problems for people using communications skills Has the demonstrated ability to prepare or revise written reports or other documents Familiarity with Microsoft Office products An offer of employment will be contingent upon the successful completion of background checks. Application Instructions: Please be prepared to attach the following documents after clicking on Apply Now button: Resume/CV Review of applications will start on immediately. The position will remain open until it is filled. For a complete job description, benefits information, and to apply online, please visit: Saint Michael's College Careers . Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 65 Job Category Health and Safety Posting Date 04/21/2026, 09:08 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations 1 Winooski Park, Colchester, VT, 05439, US Legend Jobs at a location Group of locations © Oracle Corporation Terms Legal Notices Use command and scroll to zoom the map Use two fingers to move the map 1 Winooski Park, Colchester, VT, 05439, US Copy to Clipboard Similar Jobs On Call-Dispatcher Colchester, VT, United States Posted on 03/31/2025 The Public Safety/Fire & Rescue Departments at Saint Michael's College are inviting applications for a per diem Dispatch Switchboard Operator to dispatch radio calls and operate the College switchboard. The successful candidate will be responsible for answering all incoming calls and directing calls to the appropriate party quickly, accurately, and professionally. This role receives all emergency calls for SMC campus and the surrounding community. Dispatch, switchboard, emergency services experience desirable, but we will provide training for a motivated and dependable person with demonstrated aptitude. Contact One Winooski Park Colchester, Vermont, USA 05439 Google Maps Link Phone: 802.654.2000 Resources Canvas mySMC Webmail Catalog Library Academic Calendar Faculty and Staff Resources Graduate Student Resources Prospective Students Request Info Apply Schedule a Visit Financial Aid Majors and Minors Campus Store Contact Us Alumni Giving Alumni Events Calendar Networking Seminars Reunion Get Involved Contact Us About News Events Directory Offices and Services Sexual Respect and Title IX Website HEOA Consumer Disclosures Employment Opportunities Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube © 2021  Saint Michael's College Privacy Policy Sitemap College Home Job Opportunities Staff Faculty On-Campus Student GMHEC Opportunities Human Resources Office Employee Benefits On-Campus Student Employment Accommodations About Catholic Identity Mission & Vision Diversity & Inclusion Annual Clery Safety Report I am an employee Cookies Policy Learn more Accept Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Dispatcher - Saint Michael's College Careers loaded"
